<https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/assist-iot-weather-graphs/dev>
    a dcat:Dataset ;
    dct:title "ASSIST-IoT weather (graphs variant)"@en ;
    dct:description "This is a timestamped stream of weather data collected with a Davis Vantage Pro 2 weather station installed on the building of the [Systems Research Institute, Polish Academy of Sciences](https://www.ibspan.waw.pl/en/home/). The data was collected during the [ASSIST-IoT Horizon 2020 project](https://assist-iot.eu/). The station measured several different weather parameters and transmitted them in real time at regular intervals. The measurements have rich annotations with the [SOSA/SSN](https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-ssn/) and [OM 2.0](http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/page/om-2) ontologies. The stream is very regular and the elements only differ by numeric values and timestamps. This is the graph variant, which is a timestamped graph stream compatible with the RSP Data Model.\n    \nThe dataset is a real application of RDF streaming (originally streamed over MQTT), with much richer annotations than [citypulse-traffic](https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/citypulse-traffic). On the other hand, it is perfectly regular, with no differences in structure between stream elements."@en ;
    dct:creator [ foaf:name "ASSIST-IoT Horizon 2020 project" ; foaf:homepage <https://assist-iot.eu/> ] ;
    dct:creator [ foaf:name "Piotr Sowiński" ; foaf:homepage <https://github.com/Ostrzyciel>, <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2543-9461> ] ;
    dct:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0> ;
    dct:issued "2023-05-04"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:language "en" ;
    dcat:landingPage <https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/assist-iot-weather-graphs/dev> ;
    dcat:theme eurovoc:1892 , eurovoc:6030 , eurovoc:c_7a168de0 , eurovoc:c_b12a760a ;
    dcat:temporalResolution "PT10S"^^xsd:duration ;
    rb:hasStreamElementCount "701278"^^xsd:integer ;
    dcat:distribution <https://ldes.tech/riverbench/assist-iot-weather-graphs/root.trig#EventStream> .

# The IRI of the LDES is the entry point that a client is given
<https://ldes.tech/riverbench/assist-iot-weather-graphs/root.trig#EventStream> a ldes:EventStream ;
    dct:title "ASSIST-IoT weather (graphs variant) as an LDES: the first 10 000 elements, in Jelly-RDF"@en ;
    dct:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0> ;
    dcat:accessURL <https://ldes.tech/riverbench/assist-iot-weather-graphs/root.trig> ;
    # This LDES is a view on the RiverBench Jelly distribution with 10K elements (704 KB)
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/assist-iot-weather-graphs/dev#jelly-10k> ;
    rb:hasStreamElementCount 10000 .

# No LDES for this dataset: Every element is a set of triples in the default graph with about 30 subjects: ten
# observations and their sensor, feature of interest and properties. The feature of interest, the sensor and the
# properties are the same in all elements, and no class or property singles out one subject with an IRI that is unique
# to the element. LDES 2.0 cannot identify the members (ldes:memberGraph, ldes:memberType and ldes:memberPath all need
# one identifier per message). The graph variant (assist-iot-weather-graphs) has an LDES.
<https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/assist-iot-weather/dev>
    a dcat:Dataset ;
    dct:title "ASSIST-IoT weather (triples variant)"@en ;
    dct:description "This is a timestamped stream of weather data collected with a Davis Vantage Pro 2 weather station installed on the building of the [Systems Research Institute, Polish Academy of Sciences](https://www.ibspan.waw.pl/en/home/). The data was collected during the [ASSIST-IoT Horizon 2020 project](https://assist-iot.eu/). The station measured several different weather parameters and transmitted them in real time at regular intervals. The measurements have rich annotations with the [SOSA/SSN](https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-ssn/) and [OM 2.0](http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/page/om-2) ontologies. The stream is very regular and the elements only differ by numeric values and timestamps.\n    \nThe dataset is a real application of RDF streaming (originally streamed over MQTT), with much richer annotations than [citypulse-traffic](https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/citypulse-traffic). On the other hand, it is perfectly regular, with no differences in structure between stream elements."@en ;
    dct:creator [ foaf:name "ASSIST-IoT Horizon 2020 project" ; foaf:homepage <https://assist-iot.eu/> ] ;
    dct:creator [ foaf:name "Piotr Sowiński" ; foaf:homepage <https://github.com/Ostrzyciel>, <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2543-9461> ] ;
    dct:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0> ;
    dct:issued "2023-05-04"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:language "en" ;
    dcat:landingPage <https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/assist-iot-weather/dev> ;
    dcat:theme eurovoc:1892 , eurovoc:6030 , eurovoc:c_7a168de0 , eurovoc:c_b12a760a ;
    dcat:temporalResolution "PT10S"^^xsd:duration ;
    rb:hasStreamElementCount "701278"^^xsd:integer .

<https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/citypulse-traffic-graphs/dev>
    a dcat:Dataset ;
    dct:title "CityPulse traffic (graphs variation)"@en ;
    dct:description "This is a variation of the [citypulse-traffic](https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/citypulse-traffic) dataset that was transformed into a stream of graphs, compliant with the [RSP Data Model](https://streamreasoning.org/RSP-QL/Abstract%20Syntax%20and%20Semantics%20Document/). The dataset is a processed subset of real traffic data published by the [CityPulse EU FP7 project](http://iot.ee.surrey.ac.uk:8080/index.html). The used dataset is '[Road Traffic Data](http://iot.ee.surrey.ac.uk:8080/datasets.html#traffic)', dataset-4. The dataset was processed to fix prefixes without a trailing '#' or '/'. It consists of subsequent chronologically ordered substreams of observations from each sensor. See also [the paper](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/300337751_CityBench_A_Configurable_Benchmark_to_Evaluate_RSP_Engines_Using_Smart_City_Datasets) for more details."@en ;
    dct:creator [ foaf:name "CityPulse EU FP7 project" ; foaf:homepage <http://iot.ee.surrey.ac.uk:8080/index.html> ] ;
    dct:creator [ foaf:name "Piotr Sowiński" ; foaf:homepage <https://github.com/Ostrzyciel>, <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2543-9461> ] ;
    dct:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0> ;
    dct:issued "2023-05-01"^^xsd:date ;
    dcat:landingPage <https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/citypulse-traffic-graphs/dev> ;
    dcat:theme eurovoc:3107 , eurovoc:3127 , eurovoc:6030 , eurovoc:c_b12a760a , eurovoc:c_d59e7560 ;
    dcat:temporalResolution "PT5M"^^xsd:duration ;
    rb:hasStreamElementCount "4382599"^^xsd:integer ;
    dcat:distribution <https://ldes.tech/riverbench/citypulse-traffic-graphs/root.trig#EventStream> .

# The IRI of the LDES is the entry point that a client is given
<https://ldes.tech/riverbench/citypulse-traffic-graphs/root.trig#EventStream> a ldes:EventStream ;
    dct:title "CityPulse traffic (graphs variation) as an LDES: the first 10 000 elements, in Jelly-RDF"@en ;
    dct:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0> ;
    dcat:accessURL <https://ldes.tech/riverbench/citypulse-traffic-graphs/root.trig> ;
    # This LDES is a view on the RiverBench Jelly distribution with 10K elements (3.0 MB)
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://w3id.org/riverbench/datasets/citypulse-traffic-graphs/dev#jelly-10k> ;
